hadiths[45]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1194","´﻿ Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This matter, that is, the caliphate, will always remain among the Quraysh until only two men remain in the world."
"1195","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: In government, all people are subordinate to the Quraysh, and the Muslims are subordinate to the Muslim Quraysh, and the disbelievers are subordinate to the disbelieving Quraysh (that is, they are more deserving of leadership and authority)."
"1196","Sayyiduna ‘Amir bin Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I wrote to my servant Nafi’ and sent him to Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) asking him to narrate to me what he had heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He says: In reply, he wrote that I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the evening of that Friday, the day Ma’iz Aslami was stoned, that he was saying: “This religion will always remain established until the Day of Resurrection is established or there are twelve caliphs over you, and all of them will be from the Quraysh.” (Perhaps this will also happen near the Day of Resurrection, that at one time there will be twelve caliphs of the Muslims over twelve groups.) And I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “A small group of Muslims will conquer the white palace of Kisra.” (This was a miracle, and it happened during the caliphate of Sayyiduna ‘Umar, may Allah be pleased with him.) And I heard that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Before the Day of Resurrection, liars will appear, so beware of them.” And I heard that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When Allah gives wealth to any one of you, he should first spend on himself and his family (keep them comfortable, then give to the poor).” And I heard that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I will be waiting for you at the Hawd (Pond) of Kawthar (i.e., I will arrange for you to be given water there and will be waiting for your arrival).”"
"1197","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` I went to Umm al-Mu’minin Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) and she said, “Do you know that your father will not appoint anyone as caliph?” I said, “He will not do so.” She said, “He will surely do so.” I swore that I would mention this to him. Then I remained silent; even the next morning I could not say it to him, but I felt as if I was carrying a mountain in my hand (such was the burden of the oath). Finally, I returned to him; he began asking me about the people’s condition, and I kept informing him. Then I said, “I have heard something from the people and have sworn that I will mention it to you. They think that you will not appoint anyone as caliph. If you had a shepherd for your camels or goats, and then he came to you leaving those camels and goats behind, would you not think that those animals have been ruined? In that case, the matter of people is even more important.” My saying this made him thoughtful, and for a while he kept his head bowed (pondering). Then he raised his head and said, “Allah, Glorious and Majestic, will protect His religion. If I do not appoint a caliph, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not appoint anyone as caliph. And if I do appoint a caliph, then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) appointed a caliph.” Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “By Allah, when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), I understood that he would not equate anyone with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he would not appoint a caliph.”"
"1198","Abu Hazim says: I sat with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) for five years, and I heard him narrate from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that the affairs/government of the Children of Israel used to be managed by the Prophets. Whenever a Prophet passed away, another Prophet would succeed him. And the situation is that after me there will be no Prophet, rather there will be Caliphs and they will be many. The people asked, ""Then what do you command us to do?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Fulfill the pledge of allegiance to the first one to whom you give your pledge, and give them their due right, and Allah the Exalted will question them about what He entrusted to them."
"1199","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abd Rabb al-Ka'bah says: I entered the mosque and there Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) was sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah and people were gathered around him. I also went and sat down, so he said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). We stopped at a place, and some began to set up their tents, some started shooting arrows, and some were tending to their animals, when suddenly the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called for prayer. We all gathered around him, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There has not passed any prophet before me except that it was obligatory upon him to tell his ummah the best thing that he knew for them, and to warn them against the evil that he knew. And for this ummah of yours, its first part is safety, and its last part will be trials, and there will be things you will dislike, and there will come such tribulations that each one will make the previous one seem lighter and thinner (i.e., the later tribulation will be so much greater that the earlier one will seem insignificant in comparison). And when a tribulation comes, the believer will say: In this is my destruction. Then it will pass, and another will come, and the believer will say: In this is my destruction. So whoever wishes to be saved from Hell and enter Paradise, let his death come to him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him treat people as he would love to be treated by them. And whoever gives allegiance to an imam, giving him his hand and the intention of obedience from his heart, then he must obey him if he is able. But if another comes to dispute with him, then (forbid him, and if he does not desist without fighting) strike his neck. Hearing this, I went to Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: I ask you by Allah, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? He pointed with his hand to his ears and his heart and said: My ears heard it and my heart retained it. I said: Your cousin Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) commands us to unjustly consume each other's wealth and to destroy our lives, and Allah the Exalted says: ""O you who believe! Do not consume one another's wealth unjustly, except by way of trade with mutual consent, and do not kill yourselves. Surely Allah is Merciful to you."" (An-Nisa: 29). Hearing this, Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) remained silent for a while, then said: Obey Muawiyah in that matter which is in accordance with Allah's command, and in that which is against Allah's command, do not obey Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1200","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When allegiance is pledged to two caliphs, kill the one to whom allegiance was pledged later (because his caliphate is invalid while the first caliph exists)."
"1201","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Each of you is a guardian, and each of you will be questioned about his subjects. (By guardian is meant administrator, overseer, and protector.) Then, whoever is a king is a guardian over the people, and he will be questioned about his subjects (whether he fulfilled their rights, protected their lives and property or not). And a man is a guardian over the members of his household, and he will be questioned about them. And a woman is a guardian over her husband’s house and children, and she will be questioned about them. And a servant is a guardian over his master’s wealth, and he will be questioned about it. In short, each of you is a guardian, and each of you will be questioned about his subjects."
"1202","`Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Samurah رضي الله عنه narrates that` the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said to me: O Abdur Rahman! Do not ask for any position or authority, because if you are given (authority/position) as a result of your request, you will be left to it (on your own); but if you are given it without asking (requesting), then Allah Almighty will help you."
"1203","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr! I find you weak, and I like for you what I like for myself. Do not judge between two people, and do not take charge of the property of an orphan (because there is a possibility that the orphan's wealth may be misused or consumed for your own needs, and you may be held accountable)."
"1204","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Will you not appoint me as a governor (etc.)?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his blessed hand on my shoulder and said, ""O Abu Dharr! You are weak, and this is a trust (meaning, the ruler must fulfill both the rights of the people and the rights of Allah Almighty), and on the Day of Resurrection, this position will bring nothing but disgrace and regret, except for the one who fulfills its rights and carries out his duties with truthfulness."""
"1205","´Sayyiduna Abu Burdah narrates that` Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and with me were two men from the tribe of Ash‘ari—one on my right and one on my left. Both of them requested the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to appoint them as officials, and you (peace and blessings be upon him) were using a miswak. You (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Musa (or Abdullah bin Qais)! What do you say? I said: O Messenger of Allah! By Him Who sent you as a true Prophet, they did not tell me what was in their hearts, and I did not know that they would request this position (office of service). Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: It is as if I am seeing your (peace and blessings be upon him) miswak resting on your lower lip. You (peace and blessings be upon him) said: We never appoint to office the one who asks for it, but O Abu Musa or Abdullah bin Qais! You go. So he sent him towards Yemen. Then after him, Sayyiduna Mu‘adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) was sent (so that he would also participate). When Sayyiduna Mu‘adh reached there, Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Dismount, and he spread a cushion for him. Coincidentally, there was a man there who was tied up in captivity. Sayyiduna Mu‘adh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: What is this? Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This is a Jew who became Muslim, then unfortunately became a Jew again. He adopted his evil religion. Sayyiduna Mu‘adh said: I will not sit until he is killed according to the decision of Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him). He said this three times, then Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the order and he was killed. After that, both of them mentioned the night prayer, so Sayyiduna Mu‘adh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I sleep at night and I also worship, and I hope that I will get the same reward for sleeping as I get for worship."
"1206","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): He (peace be upon him) said: The Imam is a shield behind whom the Muslims fight (against the disbelievers), and because of whom people are protected from harm (from oppressors and robbers). Then, if he commands the fear of Allah and acts justly, he will be rewarded; and if he commands otherwise, then the burden will be upon him."
"1207","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Those who act justly will be on pulpits of light at Allah the Exalted’s right side, and both of His hands are right (meaning, the weakness found in the left hand compared to the right does not apply to Allah, for He is free from all defects). And these just people are those who are just in their judgments, and just with their families and relatives, and just in whatever responsibility is given to them."
"1208","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Shumasah says: I came to Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) to ask something, so she said: “Which people are you from?” I said: “From the people of Egypt.” She said: “What is the condition of your ruler in your conflict?” (Meaning Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, whom Sayyiduna Ali Murtaza (may Allah be pleased with him) had appointed as the ruler of Egypt after removing Qais bin Sa’d.) I said: “We have not seen anything bad from him. If anyone among us lost a camel, he would give him a camel; if a slave died, he would give a slave; and if someone needed expenses, he would provide expenses.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “What happened to my brother Muhammad bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) (that he was killed, his body was thrown among the dead, and then it was burned) does not prevent me from telling you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said in this chamber: ‘O Allah! Whoever becomes a ruler over any affair of my Ummah and is harsh with them, then be harsh with him; and whoever becomes a ruler over any affair of my Ummah and is gentle with them, then be gentle with him.’”"
"1209","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Tamim al-Dari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Religion is sincerity and goodwill. We asked, ""Towards whom?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Towards Allah, His Book, His Messenger, the leaders of the Muslims, and all the Muslims. (That is, every Muslim should obey Allah, His Messenger, and his leader, and every Muslim should fulfill the rights of other Muslims.)"
"1210","'Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that' I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on establishing prayer, giving zakat, and wishing well for every Muslim."
"1211","Sayyiduna Hasan says that Ubaydullah bin Ziyad came to visit Sayyiduna Ma'qil bin Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) during the illness in which he passed away. So Sayyiduna Ma'qil (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I narrate to you a hadith which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and if I knew that I would remain alive, I would not narrate it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: There is no servant whom Allah gives authority over people, then he dies while he is deceiving his subjects, except that Allah will make Paradise forbidden for him."
"1212","It is narrated from Hasan that Sayyiduna ‘A’idh bin ‘Amr (may Allah be pleased with him), who was a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), went to ‘Ubaydullah bin Ziyad and said to him, “O my son! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ‘The worst shepherd is an unjust ruler (who destroys his subjects),’ so do not be like that.” ‘Ubaydullah said, “Sit down, for you are the husk among the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).” Sayyiduna ‘A’idh (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Is there husk among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? The husk is among those who come after and among other people.”"
"1213","Sayedna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up one day (to advise us) and spoke about dishonesty regarding war booty, and declared it to be a major sin. Then he said: I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection coming with a camel on his neck, making noise, and he says, ""O Messenger of Allah! Help me!"" and I will say, ""I have no authority; I had conveyed to you Allah’s command."" (Imam Nawawi, may Allah have mercy on him, said: That is, I cannot forgive or intercede without Allah’s command, and perhaps at first the Prophet (peace be upon him) would say this out of anger, then intercede, provided he was a monotheist.) And I should not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a horse on his neck, neighing, and he says, ""O Messenger of Allah! Help me!"" and I will say, ""I have no authority; I had already told you (i.e., in the world I conveyed Allah’s command that the punishment for dishonesty is very severe, so why did you commit dishonesty?)."" And I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection coming with a goat on his neck, bleating, and he says, ""O Messenger of Allah! Help me!"" and I will say, ""I have no authority; I had conveyed to you Allah’s command."" And I should not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a soul on his neck, crying (whom he killed in the world), then he says, ""O Messenger of Allah! Help me!"" and I will say, ""I have no authority; I had conveyed to you Allah’s command."" I should not find any of you coming with clothes on his neck, which he is wearing (which he stole in the world), or pieces of paper flying (on which rights are written against him), or other things moving (which he stole in the world), then he says, ""O Messenger of Allah! Help me!"" and I will say, ""I have no authority; I had already informed you."" And I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection coming with gold, silver, money, etc., on his neck and saying, ""O Messenger of Allah! Help me!"" and I will say, ""I have no authority; I had already informed you."""
"1214","Sayyiduna ‘Adi bin ‘Umayrah al-Kindi (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “If we appoint any person from among you to a position, and then he conceals a needle or anything more than that, it is embezzlement (ghulul), and he will bring it with him on the Day of Resurrection.” Upon hearing this, a dark-complexioned Ansari man stood up—as if I am seeing him now—and said, “O Messenger of Allah! Take back your position from me.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “What happened to you?” He replied, “I heard you say such-and-such (i.e., that even a needle will be held accountable for).” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “I say now: If we appoint anyone to a position, he should bring everything, whether little or much. Then, whatever he is given, he may take, and whatever he is not given, he should refrain from. (In this case, there will be no accountability.)”"
"1215","Sayyiduna Abu Humayd Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed a man from the tribe of Asad, who was called Ibn al-Lutbiyyah, to collect the charity and zakat from Banu Sulaym. When he returned, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took account from him. He said, “This is your wealth, and this is a gift (which people gave me).” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Why did you not sit in your father’s or mother’s house so that your gift would come to you, if you are truthful?” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed us, and after praising and glorifying Allah, he said, “I appoint one of you to a task from among the tasks that Allah has given me, then he comes and says, ‘This is your wealth and this is a gift that was given to me.’ Why did he not sit in his father’s or mother’s house so that his gift would come to him, if he is truthful? By Allah, none of you will take anything unlawfully except that he will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection carrying it on his neck. I will surely recognize some of you who will meet Allah carrying a camel that will be grunting, or a cow that will be mooing, or a goat that will be bleating.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised both his hands until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen, and he said, “O Allah! Have I conveyed (Your message)?” (Sayyiduna Abu Humayd [may Allah be pleased with him] says:) My eyes saw this and my ears heard this."
"1216","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` on the day of Hudaybiyyah, we were one thousand four hundred men and we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was holding your (peace and blessings be upon him) hand under the tree of Ridwan, and it was a samurah tree (samurah is a wild tree that grows in the desert), and we pledged allegiance to you (peace and blessings be upon him) on the condition that we would not flee, and we did not pledge allegiance that we would die."
"1217","Sayyiduna Salim bin Abi Al-Ja'd says: I asked Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) about the Companions of the Tree, how many people were they? He said: If we had been a hundred thousand people, (the well there) would have sufficed us (because by the supplication of the Prophet ﷺ, its water had greatly increased). We were fifteen hundred people."
"1218","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the people of Shajarah were thirteen hundred men, and the (tribe of) Aslam constituted one-eighth of the Muhajirun."
"1219","Yazid bin Abi Ubaid says: I asked Sayyiduna Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him), ""On what did you pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of Hudaybiyyah?"" He replied, ""We pledged allegiance to death."""
"1220","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` we used to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to listen and obey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: Say also, ""As much as I am able."" (This was the compassion of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, for his Ummah, that if something could not be done, they would not be sinful for not doing it.)"
"1221","Junadah bin Abi Umayyah says: We went to Sayyiduna ‘Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) during his illness. We said: May Allah grant you health. Narrate to us a hadith from which Allah may benefit us, and which you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called us and we pledged allegiance to him, and among the covenants he took from us was that we pledged allegiance to listen and obey, in pleasure and displeasure, in hardship and ease, and even when our rights are denied, and that we would not dispute the authority of those who are worthy of it, except if you see clear disbelief for which you have proof from Allah."
"1222","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when Muslim women used to migrate, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would test them according to this verse: “O Prophet! When believing women come to you to give you the pledge that they will not associate anything with Allah, nor will they steal, nor will they commit adultery... till the end” (Al-Mumtahina: 12). Then, any woman who acknowledged these matters would, in effect, acknowledge the pledge (i.e., the pledge would be complete). And when they would acknowledge with their tongues before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he would say, “Go, I have taken your pledge.” By Allah, the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) never touched the hand of any woman; rather, he would take the pledge from them only verbally. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not take any pledge from women except what Allah had commanded, and the Prophet’s palm never touched the palm of any woman; rather, he would only say it verbally, and when they acknowledged, he would say, “I have taken your pledge.”"
"1223","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. And whoever obeys the ruler (whom I have appointed), then he has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys him has disobeyed me."
"1224","It is narrated from Umm Husayn (may Allah be pleased with her), the grandmother of Yahya bin Husayn, that: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he said many things. Then I heard him say: If a slave whose hands and feet are cut off, and who is black, is appointed as your leader, and he leads you according to the Book of Allah, then listen to him and obey him."
"1225","It is narrated from Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent an army and appointed a man as their leader (amir). He lit a fire and told the people to enter it. Some people intended to enter it, while others said, ""We became Muslims by fleeing from the fire (and we abandoned disbelief out of fear of Hell, so how can we now enter the fire again? This is not possible for us)."" Then this matter was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said to those who intended to enter, ""If you had entered it, you would have remained in it forever (because this is suicide and forbidden in Shariah)."" And he praised those who were not willing to enter and said, ""There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah; rather, obedience is only in what is permissible."""
"1226","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): He (peace be upon him) said: It is obligatory upon a Muslim to listen to and obey (the ruler), whether he likes it or not, except when he is ordered to commit a sin; in that case, he should neither listen nor obey."
"1227","Wa'il al-Hadrami says that Salamah bin Zaid Jufi (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""O Noble Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! If our leaders are appointed who demand their rights from us but do not give us our rights, what do you command us to do?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned away (i.e., did not answer). He asked again, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) still did not answer. Then, when he asked a second or third time, Ash'ath bin Qais dragged Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ""Listen and obey. The burden of their deeds is upon them and the burden of your deeds is upon you."" In another narration, it is mentioned that Ash'ath bin Qais dragged him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Listen and obey. Their deeds are with them and your deeds are with you."""
"1228","Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The best of your rulers are those whom you love and they love you, and they pray for you and you pray for them. And the worst of your rulers are those whom you hate and they hate you, you curse them and they curse you."" The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Should we not fight such evil rulers with the sword?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""No, as long as they establish prayer among you. And when you see something from your rulers that you dislike, then dislike their action, but do not withdraw from their obedience (i.e., do not rebel)."""
"1229","Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “There will be rulers appointed over you, and you will see both good and bad deeds from them. Whoever recognizes the bad deed as evil has protected himself from sin, and whoever speaks against it is also safe, but whoever is pleased with it and follows it (is destroyed).” The people asked, “O Messenger of Allah! Should we fight against them?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “No, as long as they establish prayer.” To speak against it means to dislike it in the heart and to consider it evil in the heart (even if one cannot say it with the tongue)."
"1230","Narrated from Sayyiduna Usaid bin Hudair (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man from the Ansar separated himself and said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Will you not appoint me as an official (governor or collector) like you have appointed such-and-such person?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me, you will be deprived of your rights, so be patient until you meet me at the Hawd (Pond) of Kawthar."""
"1231","`Sayyiduna Hudhayfah bin al-Yaman (may Allah be pleased with him) says:` People used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about good things, but I used to ask about evil out of fear that I might fall into it. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We were in ignorance and evil, then Allah brought us this good (i.e., Islam). Will there be any evil after this good?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Yes, but there will be a stain in it."" I said, ""What will that stain be?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""There will be people who will follow a way other than my Sunnah and will follow guidance other than my guidance. Among them will be good things and bad things."" I said, ""Will there be evil after that?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Yes, there will be people who will call towards the doors of Hell. Whoever responds to them, they will throw him into Hell."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Describe those people to us."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""They will have our complexion and will speak our language (i.e., they will be from among us)."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What should I do if I reach that time?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Stick to the group of Muslims and their Imam."" I said, ""What if there is no group and no Imam?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then keep away from all those sects, even if you have to bite the root of a tree, and remain in that state until death overtakes you."""
"1232","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: Whoever withdraws from obedience to the ruler and separates from the community, then dies in that state, his death will be like the death of the days of ignorance. And whoever fights under a blind banner (i.e., a battle whose legitimacy is not clearly established by Shariah), becomes angry for tribalism, calls towards tribalism, or supports tribalism (and does not seek Allah’s pleasure), then if he is killed, his killing will be like that of the days of ignorance. And whoever attacks my Ummah, killing the good and the bad alike, not sparing even the believer, and does not fulfill the covenant made with anyone, then he has nothing to do with me and I have nothing to do with him (i.e., he is not a Muslim)."
"1233","Nafi’ says that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) came to Abdullah bin Muti’ when the incident of Harrah occurred during the time of Yazid bin Muawiyah (he sent an army to Madinah, and the people of Madinah were killed at Harrah, which is a place adjacent to Madinah, and various kinds of oppression were inflicted upon the people of Madinah). Abdullah bin Muti’ said, “Lay down a cushion or mattress for Abu Abdur Rahman (this is the kunyah of Abdullah bin Umar).” He said, “I have not come to sit with you, but rather to narrate to you a hadith which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ‘Whoever removes his hand from obedience will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with no proof for himself, and whoever dies without having pledged allegiance to anyone, his death will be like the death of the days of ignorance.’”"
"1234","Sayyiduna Arfajah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, ""Trials and turmoil are near. Then whoever seeks to disrupt the unity of this Ummah, whoever he may be, kill him."""
"1235","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever raises a weapon against us is not from among us, and whoever deceives us is also not from among us."
"1236","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty likes three things for you and dislikes three things. He likes that you worship Him and do not associate anyone with Him, and that you all hold fast to His rope (the Book and the Sunnah) together and do not be divided. And Allah Almighty dislikes idle talk, excessive questioning (i.e., asking about matters that are unnecessary or not needed, or questions that may be unpleasant to others), and wasting wealth (He dislikes it, such as in innovations, drinking alcohol, gambling, smoking, kite flying, fireworks, etc.)."
"1237","Sa’d bin Ibrahim says: I asked Qasim bin Muhammad about a man who has three houses and he made a bequest of one-third (of each house) in each house. He said that the three thirds will be combined in one house. Then he said that Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) informed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever does an act for which we have not given a command (i.e., introduces a new practice in the religion), it is rejected."
"1238","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that it was said to him, ""Do you not go to Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) and speak to him?"" He replied, ""Do you think I do not speak to him? Should I not let you hear? By Allah, I have spoken to him about matters between me and him. However, I did not wish to be the first to open a matter that someone else would open before me, and I do not say to anyone who is in authority over me that he is the best among all people (i.e., I do not flatter). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: On the Day of Resurrection, a man will be brought and thrown into Hell. His intestines will come out and he will go around with them as a donkey goes around a millstone. The people of Hell will gather around him and ask, 'O so-and-so! What happened to you? Did you not command good and forbid evil?' He will say, 'I used to command good to others but did not do it myself, and I used to forbid evil to others but did not refrain from it myself.'"""
